&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The
     waste facilities provided is inadequate with regard to the proposed 1x3 bed flat and the details associated with
     the refuse provision is considered to be insufficient. The development
     therefore is contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the
     National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D6 of the London Plan
     (2021), Core Policy CS.1X of the Harrow Core Strategy, Policies DM44 and
     DM45 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The
     proposal fails to provide adequate fire safety measures, including appropriate
     fire escapes/safety routes, contrary to the high quality design
     aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024) and Policies
     D11 and D12 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
 &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;The
     proposed two storey rear extension, by reason of its excessive cumulative
     depth, height and siting, and raised platform, would be detrimental to the
     amenities of the neighbouring occupiers at No. 115 Headstone Road,
     contrary to Policies D3.D(7) and D14 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM1
     of the Development Management Policies Local Plan document (2013) and the
     relevant provisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document
     Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top:0cm&quot; start=&quot;1&quot; type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
